BEGIN:VEVENT
DESCRIPTION:Intervenant·e : Eugenio VERRINA\nÉtablissement : Université Lumière Lyon 2\, GATE\nMots-clés : économie expérimentale et comportementale\, raisonnement motivé et normes sociales\n\nRésumé :\nSelection neglect and correlation neglect\, i.e.\, the failure to account for selection and correlation in the information one receives\, lead to biased beliefs and are two key drivers behind belief polarization. Social identity is often embedded in environments with selected and correlated signals\, with echo chambers as a prime example. In these contexts\, people inside one’s echo chamber can be perceived as part of one's in-group\, e.g.\, because of a shared political affiliation\, while people outside one's echo chamber can be perceived as part of one's out-group. We study how the combination of social identity and selection neglect or correlation neglect affects belief formation. We design a novel experimental paradigm where receivers guess a randomly-generated number based on the estimates of multiple senders. We manipulate i) whether the signal structure can induce selection neglect or correlation neglect\, and ii) the presence of social identities. We find that selection neglect is exacerbated when the omitted signals are from out-group senders. In contrast\, if the omitted signals are from in-group senders\, subjects become better at accounting for selection. Similarly\, correlation neglect worsens when in-group signals are correlated\, while it improves when correlation is on the out-group. Moreover\, we show that social identity alone causes no bias\, suggesting it is the combination of selection neglect or correlation neglect with social identity that drives our results. Finally\, we provide some evidence for the mechanisms underlying our results. Our findings offer insights into the determinants of polarization and have important implications for the design of information structure and of policies aimed at reducing it. Le séminaire a lieu à 11h15\, au GAEL. Date Le 17 septembre 2026 Localisation Complément lieu salle 227 Imprimer Partager Partager sur Facebook Partager sur LinkedIn Partager l'URL de cette page Publié le 11 septembre 2026 Mis à jour le 16 septembre 2026 🔵 Laboratoire GAEL 1241 rue des Résidences 38400 Saint-Martin-d'Hères 04 76 74 29 26 - gael-admin@inrae.fr 🔵 Pour joindre la plateforme d'économie expérimentale : gael-ecoexp@univ-grenoble-alpes.fr Menu footer Contact Plan du site Crédits Mentions légales Données personnelles Gestion des cookies Accessibilité : non conforme Se connecter Suivez-nous ! Facebook LinkedIn\n\nProgramme GAEL : https://gael.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/fr/calendrier-2026-2027-0\nPage du séminaire : https://gael.univ-grenoble-alpes.fr/fr/actualites/eugenio-verrina-professeur-luniversite-lumiere-lyon-2-et-chercheur-au-gate
DURATION:PT1H15M
LOCATION:GAEL\, salle 227
DTSTART:20260917T091500Z
SUMMARY:Belief formation and social Identity
UID:13b7cb642fa028705245bdf9@gael-seminars
